lede: 'A casino doesn''t know who will win the next spin, and it doesn''t need to. It has a small edge on every bet and millions of bets. Quant trading firms run the same arithmetic on markets: models find small edges, machines trade them thousands of times a day, and the law of large numbers turns "slightly better than a coin" into a business. The hard part is that, unlike a casino, a trading firm has to find its edge, prove it''s real, and keep it from being copied.'
